    "id": "friction_comparison",
    "prerequisites": ["ramp", "spinning_shapes"],
    "suggested_order": 90,
    "summary": "In the upper lanes, equal blocks slide along or across the preferred direction of a surface. In the lower lanes, equal balls roll with and without rolling and spinning resistance. They all start at the same speed. Contact with the surface slows them, and a low stop ends each lane.",
    "title": "Friction and rolling"
  },
